        "text": "<p><br/>The range stays small by design. Adding something new usually means taking<br/>something else away, and that rule has saved us from a lot of mediocre<br/>products. We look for things that are made from one honest material, that<br/>do not need replacing, and that do one job properly.<br/><br/>Nothing gets listed before we have had it in our hands. We buy it, use it,<br/>and look for the things a product photo never shows: how it feels after a<br/>week, whether it stains, whether it is annoying to clean. If it disappoints<br/>us, it does not go on the site. That is also why restocks sometimes take a<br/>few weeks: we would rather be out of stock than quietly swap in something<br/>else.<br/><br/></p>",
